---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Salary Negotiation Tool — No Signup, No Login, Free | SalaryPitcher"
  description="Use a free salary negotiation tool with no signup required. Generate counter offer emails, compare offers, and calculate your worth instantly."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Salary Negotiation Tool (No Signup)", path: "/salary-negotiation-no-signup" },
  ]}
>
  <!-- FAQPage Schema JSON-LD -->
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I really not need to sign up to use the salary negotiation tool?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Correct. There is no account, no email, and no login. Open the tool, answer a few questions, and generate your negotiation email right in the browser."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What can I do with a no-signup salary negotiation tool?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "You can generate a personalized counter offer email, see a market-backed salary range for your role and location, compare up to five job offers side by side, and calculate your net take-home pay — all without creating an account."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a no-signup salary tool less accurate than a paid one?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. The market data comes from Bureau of Labor Statistics wage surveys for your role and metro area. Being free and login-free does not reduce the quality of the data or the email drafts."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is my information stored anywhere?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Because there is no account system, the answers you enter never leave your browser until you choose to send the generated email yourself. Nothing is saved on our servers."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  </script>

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto w-full space-y-8">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="text-center space-y-4 py-4">
      <div
        class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider bg-accent-blue/15 text-accent-blue border border-accent-blue/10"
      >
        No Signup · No Login · Free
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink leading-tight">
        Free Salary Negotiation Tool — No Signup Required
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-body max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        Most salary tools lock the useful parts behind a signup wall. This one
        does not. Open the tool, answer a handful of questions, and get a
        market-backed negotiation email — no account, no email, no credit card.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/pitch-assistant"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-8 py-3.5 bg-ink text-canvas hover:bg-ink/90 font-medium rounded-full text-sm transition-all duration-300 cursor-pointer ripple-btn btn-press"
      >
        Start Negotiating — No Signup →
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Why no signup matters -->
    <section class="border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-lg shadow-sm p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight">
        Why a No-Signup Salary Negotiation Tool Matters
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        Job offers come with deadlines. The last thing you want when a recruiter
        is waiting for a response is a 10-minute account creation flow and a
        marketing email list. A no-signup tool lets you go from "I have an
        offer" to "here is my counter email" in the time it takes to finish a
        coffee.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        It also removes the friction that causes most people to skip
        negotiating altogether. When the tool is instantly accessible, you are
        far more likely to actually send a counter — and sending one is worth,
        on average, an extra
        <strong class="text-ink">7-20% of your salary</strong>. That is
        thousands of dollars per year, and it compounds across every future
        raise and job change built on top of your starting base.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        Beyond the email generator, this no-signup suite includes a
        <a
          href="/offer-comparison"
          class="text-accent-blue hover:underline font-semibold"
          >job offer comparison tool</a
        >
        that lets you weigh up to five offers side by side, and a
        <a
          href="/salary-calculator"
          class="text-accent-blue hover:underline font-semibold"
          >salary calculator</a
        >
        that estimates your net take-home pay. Every tool works without an
        account.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- How to use -->
    <section class="border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-lg shadow-sm p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight">
        How to Use the Tool Without Creating an Account
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">1. Enter your role and offer</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            Pick your job title, location, and experience level, then type in
            the salary you were offered. The tool immediately calculates a
            market range so you can see where you stand.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">2. Add your achievement</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            Describe your strongest measurable result in at least 30 words. This
            becomes the justification baked into your email draft.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">3. Generate and send</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            Choose your tone, review the draft, and copy it into your email
            client. Nothing is stored — your details leave your browser only
            when you press send.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Privacy & trust -->
    <section class="border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-lg shadow-sm p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight">
        What Happens to Your Data
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        Because the tool has no login, there is no profile, no saved history,
        and no email marketing list to join. The details you enter are used only
        to build your email on the spot. For more on how we handle information,
        read our
        <a href="/privacy" class="text-accent-blue hover:underline font-semibold"
          >privacy policy</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        If you are new to the process and want strategy before you draft, start
        with our guide on
        <a
          href="/guides/how-to-negotiate-salary-after-job-offer"
          class="text-accent-blue hover:underline font-semibold"
          >how to negotiate salary after a job offer</a
        >, then use the no-signup tool to turn that strategy into a polished
        email.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- More tools -->
    <section class="border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-lg shadow-sm p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight">
        More No-Signup Salary Tools in the Suite
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        The negotiation email is just the starting point. This site is a full
        no-signup salary toolkit, and every tool is free:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink">Pitch Assistant</strong> — the core
          negotiation email generator that turns your role, offer, and
          achievement into a complete counter.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="/offer-comparison"
            class="text-accent-blue hover:underline font-semibold"
            >Offer comparison tool</a
          >
          — line up to five job offers side by side with base, equity, bonus,
          and cost-of-living adjustments.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="/salary-calculator"
            class="text-accent-blue hover:underline font-semibold"
            >Salary calculator</a
          >
          — convert hourly to annual and estimate federal take-home pay.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="/company-salaries"
            class="text-accent-blue hover:underline font-semibold"
            >Company salary explorer</a
          >
          — see compensation at Google, Meta, Amazon, and other top employers.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        Unlike platforms that collect your email and then bury the useful
        features behind a paywall, everything here works immediately — no
        account creation, no credit card, no email capture.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Comparison to paid -->
    <section class="border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-lg shadow-sm p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight">
        How This Tool Compares to Paid Negotiation Services
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        Paid negotiation coaches and services can be worth the money for
        executive-level packages, but most candidates do not need one. The core
        of a successful counter — market data, a clear achievement, and a
        polite, specific ask — is exactly what this free, no-signup tool
        provides.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        The data is the same Bureau of Labor Statistics source used by many paid
        services, and the generated email is fully editable. Spend the money
        (and the time) only if you have a genuinely complex package with equity,
        retention bonuses, or unusual terms. For a standard offer, start here.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        If you are weighing whether a competing offer changes your strategy, the
        free
        <a
          href="/offer-comparison"
          class="text-accent-blue hover:underline font-semibold"
          >offer comparison tool</a
        >
        can show the real dollar difference between packages after equity and
        cost-of-living adjustments — leverage you can then use in your counter
        email.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        Before you open the tool, spend three minutes reviewing
        <a
          href="/guides/salary-negotiation-mistakes"
          class="text-accent-blue hover:underline font-semibold"
          >10 salary negotiation mistakes to avoid</a
        >
        — avoiding the common errors is worth more than any template.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section
      class="p-6 border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-lg shadow-sm flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-between items-center gap-6"
    >
      <div class="space-y-1 text-center sm:text-left">
        <p class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm">
          No account. No waiting. Just your counter.
        </p>
        <p class="text-xs text-mute">
          Generate a market-backed negotiation email in about two minutes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a
        href="/pitch-assistant"
        class="px-6 py-2.5 bg-ink text-canvas hover:bg-ink/90 font-medium rounded-full text-xs transition-colors shrink-0 ripple-btn btn-press"
      >
        Use the Tool Now →
      </a>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-lg shadow-sm p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-5">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight">
        Salary Negotiation Tool — FAQ
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink mb-1">
            Do I really not need to sign up?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            Correct. There is no account, no email, and no login. Open the tool
            and start generating right in the browser.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink mb-1">
            What can I do with a no-signup salary negotiation tool?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            Generate a personalized counter offer email, see a market-backed
            salary range, compare up to five offers, and estimate take-home pay —
            all without creating an account.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink mb-1">
            Is a no-signup salary tool less accurate than a paid one?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            No. The market data comes from Bureau of Labor Statistics wage
            surveys for your role and metro area.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink mb-1">
            Is my information stored anywhere?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            No. Because there is no account system, nothing is saved on our
            servers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
